uous on it because it is not defined at $x=0$ (it makes zero the denominator).   Therefore, the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval  $[0,1)$   is not closed, so the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $[-2,-1]$    is closed, and the function is continuous on $[-2,-1].$   Therefore, the extreme value theorem is applicable.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"III only\"." 13194139534501 true] [17592186292146 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292147 13194139534501 true] [17592186292146 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292148 13194139534501 true] [17592186292146 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292149 13194139534501 true] [17592186292146 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292150 13194139534501 true] [17592186292146 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292151 13194139534501 true] [17592186292146 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534501 true] [17592186292146 1041 "selection" 13194139534501 true] [17592186292146 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292149 13194139534501 true] [17592186292146 1110 #uuid "80572577-9095-53b4-ae8f-965587b22bc6" 13194139534501 true] [17592186292147 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534501 true] [17592186292147 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534501 true] [17592186292147 1111 #uuid "2b82ea67-b6cf-5760-bf11-14d7edd39c05" 13194139534501 true] [17592186292148 1034 "I only" 13194139534501 true] [17592186292148 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534501 true] [17592186292148 1111 #uuid "2d87a897-20df-53d1-bc74-6d84e2af38c6" 13194139534501 true] [17592186292149 1034 "III only" 13194139534501 true] [17592186292149 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534501 true] [17592186292149 1111 #uuid "aff24036-7855-57a0-8fca-61d0d66febcb" 13194139534501 true] [17592186292150 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534501 true] [17592186292150 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534501 true] [17592186292150 1111 #uuid "efe0b73c-d92b-5f79-847c-85c109010815" 13194139534501 true] [17592186292151 1034 "II only" 13194139534501 true] [17592186292151 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534501 true] 